## Microsoft Intune — Windows 11 MDM Enrollment 
09212026
### Objective

Extend the existing `aden.local` Active Directory / Microsoft Entra ID lab by enrolling a domain-joined Windows 11 Enterprise workstation into Microsoft Intune for MDM management.

### Architecture

```text
Windows Server 2022
Active Directory (aden.local)
        │
        │ Entra Connect
        ▼
Microsoft Entra ID
        │
        ▼
Microsoft Intune
        │
        │ MDM
        ▼
Windows 11 Enterprise
```

### 1. Troubleshoot Group Policy

Windows Settings was inaccessible due to an existing `Restrict Control Panel` GPO.

Identify applied policies:

```cmd
gpresult /r
```

After removing the restrictive GPO, refresh policy on the Windows 11 client:

```cmd
gpupdate /force
```

Verified that Windows Settings was accessible after the policy refresh.

### 2. Create a Dedicated Admin Account

Created a separate administrative account in Active Directory:

```text
ADEN\svadmin
```

Rather than granting administrative privileges to the normal user account, `svadmin` is used for workstation administration.

Added the account to the Windows 11 client's local Administrators group:

```cmd
net localgroup Administrators "ADEN\svadmin" /add
```

Verify membership:

```cmd
net localgroup Administrators
```

Verify current logged-in identity:

```cmd
whoami
```

This provides workstation administrative privileges without granting Domain Admin permissions.

### 3. Configure an Intune Test User

Used a standard AD user representing an employee:

```text
ADEN\jsmith
```

The account was synchronized into Microsoft Entra ID through Entra Connect:

```text
ADEN\jsmith
      │
      │ Entra Connect
      ▼
jsmith@<tenant>.onmicrosoft.com
```

Assigned the synchronized user a **Microsoft Intune Plan 1** license through the Microsoft 365 Admin Center.

### 4. Enroll Windows 11 into Intune

Logged into the Windows 11 workstation using:

```text
ADEN\svadmin
```

Navigated to:

```text
Settings
→ Accounts
→ Access work or school
→ Enroll only in device management
```

Authenticated using the Intune-licensed employee account:

```text
jsmith@<tenant>.onmicrosoft.com
```

### 5. Verify MDM Enrollment

Windows successfully reported:

```text
Connected by jsmith@<tenant>.onmicrosoft.com
Connected to Default Directory MDM
Managed by Default Directory
```

The workstation simultaneously remained joined to:

```text
aden.local
```

Final architecture:

```text
             Microsoft Entra ID
                    │
              Microsoft Intune
                    │
                   MDM
                    │
                    ▼
             Windows 11 Client
                    ▲
                    │
              Domain Joined
                    │
               aden.local
                    │
           Windows Server 2022
```

### Troubleshooting Commands

Check applied Group Policy:

```cmd
gpresult /r
```

Generate detailed Group Policy report:

```cmd
gpresult /h C:\gp-report.html
```

Force Group Policy refresh:

```cmd
gpupdate /force
```

Verify domain user:

```cmd
net user jsmith /domain
```

Add domain admin account to local Administrators:

```cmd
net localgroup Administrators "ADEN\svadmin" /add
```

View local administrators:

```cmd
net localgroup Administrators
```

Check current identity:

```cmd
whoami
```

Check Entra/device registration status:

```cmd
dsregcmd /status
```

